      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We reviewed our experience with adenosine for the conversion of paroxysmal supraventricular tachycardia (PSVT) to determine whether the recommended dosing strategy of 6 mg, followed by 12 mg, is cost-effective in actual practice. We observed a 65% conversion rate to sinus rhythm with the initial dosage of 6 mg adenosine (95% CI, 54% to 75%), and, based on subsequent cost analysis, conclude that the current strategy should not be replaced by a 12-mg-first strategy. If the packaging of adenosine was changed so that 12 mg cost less than twice 6 mg, this analysis should be revisited."},
